From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Say what the firewall check found

Setting the firewall up for a cast asks firewalld three things in turn, and
reported none of them. Every step that failed returned its error to the
caller without a word in the log, including the one case that is not an
answer from firewalld at all but a deadline running out on this side. A cast
that stopped at the firewall left behind a single line, written by the sink,
that said the zone was missing. That line was true about what the sink had
been told and said nothing about which of the three calls had failed, or
why, and reading the zone turned out to be a different problem from the one
it described.

Each step now says what came of it: which zones were asked for, whether the
one that is wanted was among them, whether it had to be created, and whether
firewalld loaded it. The failures say so too, and the one that comes from
this side names the error domain and code, so a deadline that ran out cannot
be mistaken for a refusal by firewalld again.

Nothing about what the code does changes. How long each step took is left to
the timestamps the log already carries.

diff -ruN a/src/nd-firewalld.c b/src/nd-firewalld.c
--- a/src/nd-firewalld.c
+++ b/src/nd-firewalld.c
@@ -50,10 +50,13 @@
   val = g_dbus_connection_call_finish (connection, res, &error);
   if (!val)
     {
+      g_warning ("NdFirewalld: Could not get firewalld to load the zone: %s", error->message);
       g_task_return_error (task, error);
       return;
     }
 
+  g_debug ("NdFirewalld: Firewalld loaded the zone; the firewall is ready.");
+
   /* Assume everything is fine (though, we should maybe double check the configuration). */
   g_task_return_boolean (task, TRUE);
 }
@@ -71,10 +74,13 @@
   val = g_dbus_connection_call_finish (connection, res, &error);
   if (!val)
     {
+      g_warning ("NdFirewalld: Could not create the zone: %s", error->message);
       g_task_return_error (task, error);
       return;
     }
 
+  g_debug ("NdFirewalld: Created the zone; asking firewalld to load it.");
+
   /* We created a zone, but it will not be loaded yet. We also need to
    * trigger a reload after doing this. */
   cancellable = g_task_get_cancellable (task);
@@ -211,6 +217,12 @@
           return;
         }
 
+      /* Not an answer from firewalld but a failure on this side, which is
+       * where a deadline that ran out ends up. Saying so is the difference
+       * between a report that names the cause and one that does not. */
+      g_warning ("NdFirewalld: Could not ask firewalld for the zone names: %s (%s %d)",
+                 error->message, g_quark_to_string (error->domain), error->code);
+
       g_task_return_error (task, error);
       return;
     }
@@ -223,12 +235,13 @@
     {
       if (g_str_equal (zones[i], ND_WFD_ZONE))
         {
+          g_message ("NdFirewalld: Firewalld named the %s zone; nothing to set up.", ND_WFD_ZONE);
           g_task_return_boolean (task, TRUE);
           return;
         }
     }
 
-  g_debug ("NdFirewalld: The zone is not there yet; will create it.");
+  g_message ("NdFirewalld: The zone is not there yet; will create it.");
   create_wfd_zone (g_steal_pointer (&task), connection);
 }
 
@@ -256,6 +269,8 @@
       return;
     }
 
+  g_message ("NdFirewalld: Asking firewalld which zones it has.");
+
   g_dbus_connection_call (connection,
                           FIREWALLD_NAME,
                           FIREWALLD_PATH,
